{
  "_doc": "---------------------------------------------------------------- ANIMALS\nlivestock + working animals as DATA. `gives` maps a product -> yield; `eats` is the feed; matures\nand lifespan are in the sim's months (one month = TIME.days_per_year / 12 = 30 days; one period is one\nday). A draught animal has a `pull` (the weight it can haul).\n\nLIFE CYCLE (Phase 008). `founding_sex` is the sex of an animal the founding town is given (or of one\nadded without a stated sex). `breeds` false means the species does not breed pairwise in this model (a\nbee colony is one animal here, and its growth is not modelled). For a breeding species:\n  gestation_days         days from conception to birth (a chicken's 21 days is the incubation of\n                         a clutch; the model treats hatching as the birth)\n  litter                 young per birth (an integer average; the model does not draw litter sizes)\n  breeding_interval_days the least days from one conception to the next (a dam is not bred again\n                         until this has passed; it covers the gestation and the rest after a birth)\n  birth_male_share       the share of births that are male (drawn from the animal-life stream)\n`approx` names the life-cycle figures that are APPROX: they are recalled from the standard references\nbelow and were not re-checked against the texts (no source access in Phase 008). The references are\nHafez & Hafez, Reproduction in Farm Animals (7th ed., 2000), for livestock gestation and litter\nfigures; the Merck Veterinary Manual's companion-animal and poultry sections for dog, cat, and\nchicken; and standard dairy and sheep husbandry practice for the calving and lambing intervals.\nPig lifespan (supervisor, Phase 008): 180 months (15 years, APPROX), corrected from 15; the other species' lifespans are natural lifespans in months, and 15 months made a fed founding pig die of old age on day 270.",
